2026-09-19: WI-C5-01 Done: external inspection facade over the C4 pipeline. Public immutable ExternalAssetCatalog (display name, format, scene/node/primitive/vertex/index/material/image/skin/joint counts, box+sphere bounds, required/optional feature ids, animation descriptors, non-fatal diagnostics) with defensive copies against input mutation; ExternalAnimationDescriptor carries the stable <model>#animation=<index> key plus the name/duration/channel-count the real import produces; ExternalAssetInspectionDiagnostic (code/severity/message). Public IExternalAssetInspector.InspectModel(key, context) returns null for invalid key/missing root exactly like the importers. ExternalAssetInspection.SelectFormat selects by final extension (.gltf/.glb case-insensitive, anything else EXT001 UnsupportedFormat with no exception), returning immutable ExternalFormatSelection (format id + GltfImportOptions + inspector; exposes neither C1 importer interface, reflection-checked). Internal ExternalFormatFactory maps the GLTF identifier to GltfModelImporter/GltfAnimationImporter with one explicit entry and no registry. GltfExternalAssetInspector mirrors the importer orchestration with shared policy: same GltfDocumentLoader/resolver, ValidateExtensionPolicy (optional extensions -> GLTF0001 warnings), EnforceDocumentLimits/EnforcePrimitiveLimits (extracted to internal static, options parameterized), same scene plan, per-primitive GltfMaterialConverter conversion (material/image distinct counts), GltfPrimitiveConverter/GltfSkinConverter for vertices/indices/bounds parity with the imported mesh (test asserts equality against a real GltfModelImporter import), no-convertible-geometry rejection with the importer's message, and per-animation GltfAnimationConverter runs for descriptor parity. 20 ExternalAssetInspectionTests: selection matrix incl. double-suffixed/compound/empty, options passthrough, null boundaries, static-model parity vs importer, animation-descriptor parity + key round-trip through GltfAssetKey, limit parity, no-geometry parity, immutability, no-SharpGLTF-typed public surface, factory mapping. WI-C5-02 and WI-C5-03 flipped to Ready. Validation: 20/20 new tests, full non-interactive suite green (1393+204+53), build/format/brace clean; unrelated PbrMaterialProof test-root probe fixed to accept linked-worktree .git files.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-02 Done: disposable external source mounts. New public OpenSage.IO ExternalSourceFileSystem (FileSystem over one DiskFileSystem): validates virtual keys before any delegation - null/empty (file keys), rooted, alternate separator '\', leading slash, ':' drive/scheme separator, empty segments (repeated separators, trailing slash), dot segments, and whitespace-only segments all throw InvalidDataException; missing files still return null. Containment enforced twice: lexical Path.GetFullPath pre-check, then physical per-segment resolution through DirectoryInfo/FileInfo.ResolveLinkTarget(returnFinalTarget) on returned entries so symlinked files or intermediate directories that leave the canonical root at any hop are rejected (enumeration filters escapees instead of throwing). Platform-appropriate root comparison (OrdinalIgnoreCase on Windows, Ordinal otherwise). Disposal disposes the delegated DiskFileSystem and is idempotent; access after dispose throws ObjectDisposedException. New public ExternalAssetSourceMount (OpenSage.Game) from an absolute selected file: requires an absolute path naming a file, canonicalizes the directory as CanonicalRootPath, selected file name becomes RootVirtualKey, runs ExternalAssetInspection.SelectFormat (unsupported -> InvalidDataException carrying EXT001), and owns one ExternalSourceFileSystem + AssetImportContext; model and animation mounts are independent instances, never combined with CompositeFileSystem or the game installation. 16 ExternalSourceFileSystemTests: nested relatives, root/subdirectory enumeration, all rejected forms, case behavior through the DiskFileSystem fallback, symlink escape (file), independent roots, disposed access, mount root-key/context/EXT001/absolute-path requirements, mount independence, idempotent dispose. WI-C5-03 flip to Done follows its own commit; C5-04 becomes Ready once both land. Validation: 46/46 combined new Game.Tests, full non-interactive suite green, build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-03 Done: structured diagnostics, deterministic failure mapping, eligibility, and the versioned report contract in ReplaySketch.Core (Model/ExternalModels). Enums: severity Info/Warning/Error, stage Selection/Resolve/Parse/Convert/Validate/Materialize/Bind/Render, source role Model/Animation. ExternalModelDiagnostic: immutable, identity = Code+Source+Context+Message (Equals/GetHashCode), OccurrenceCount >= 1, [JsonIgnore] ExceptionDetail. ExternalModelDiagnosticMapper: one explicit table keyed by stage and exception type without touching message text - InvalidDataException -> EXT002/EXT020/GLTF010/GLTF020/IMP010/PBR010/ANIM010/GPU010 and NotSupportedException -> EXT003/EXT021/GLTF011/GLTF021/IMP011/PBR011/ANIM011/GPU011 by stage, any other exception -> EXT999 InternalFailure (Error, exception retained as local detail, message names the exception type); SortAndCollapse orders severity-desc then stage then source then context (ordinal, null first) then code with stable ties, collapsing duplicates with summed occurrence counts. PreviewEligibility: CanRender + distinct sorted BlockingDiagnosticCodes + MissingCapabilities; warnings alone never block (tested), errors and missing capabilities do. ExternalSourceIdentity: DisplayName/VirtualKey/ByteLength/SHA-256 ContentHash with Create computing the hash while restoring stream position. ExternalModelReport: schemaVersion const 1, model/animation identities, engine-owned catalog, diagnostics stored pre-sorted and collapsed, eligibility defaults to NotEvaluated. ExternalModelReportJson: camelCase + omit-nulls + indended serialization through explicit payloads (catalog counts, flattened bounds floats, animation descriptors with durationSeconds, diagnostics without exception detail); Parse returns the JsonDocument for round-trip checks. 26 ExternalModelContractTests: all 16 stage/type mappings, EXT999 retention, deterministic ordering, collapse counts, warning/error/capability eligibility, versioned round trip, forbidden-field omission (no exceptionDetail/stackTrace/secret text/rootPath property; modelSource property set is exactly displayName/virtualKey/byteLength/contentHash), stable 64-hex hashes, position restore. C5-04 flipped to Ready (C5-01+02+03 all Done). Validation: 26/26 new tests, full non-interactive suite green (1393+204+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-04 Done: graphics-free external model session in ReplaySketch.Core. ExternalModelSessionState (Empty/Inspecting/Ready/Rendering/Failed/Disposed); immutable ExternalModelSnapshot (generation, state, source display name, catalog, diagnostics, eligibility, preview-artifact metadata with no paths) + ExternalPreviewArtifactMetadata. Interfaces so Core tests need no disk or graphics: IExternalSourceMount (root key + ExternalFormatSelection + AssetImportContext), IExternalAssetSourceMountFactory (mount creation, EXT001/creation failures throw), IExternalModelArtifactStore/IExternalModelArtifactLease (one active lease per store; failed reports preserved until the next request). Production ExternalModelArtifactStore owns exactly one directory under PlatformPaths.CacheBase with fixed artifact names and deletes only that directory on dispose. ExternalModelSession: LoadModelAsync cancels current work, increments one monotonic generation, disposes prior mount and artifact lease, publishes Inspecting (then with the mount's root key), and awaits Task.Run inspection through the selection's public inspector; mount-creation failures map through the Selection stage (EXT001 surfaces in the message, EXT002 code), inspection exceptions through Parse (GLTF010/GLTF011/EXT999 with retained detail), null catalog -> EXT002, catalog warnings -> Warning diagnostics with Ready retained and eligibility unaffected; stale generations are discarded; OperationCanceledException produces no diagnostic; snapshots are published complete and in order under the gate (reentrant event). ReloadAsync re-inspects the same mount under a new generation. AdoptPreviewArtifact is generation-checked, disposes stale or prior leases, and updates artifact metadata. Dispose is idempotent, cancels, increments the generation, disposes mount/lease/store exactly once, publishes Disposed, and later operations throw ObjectDisposedException. 15 ExternalModelSessionTests with fake mounts/inspectors/stores/leases: event ordering, warnings-Ready, EXT001 selection failure, missing root, parse mapping, EXT999 retention, stale completion discard via blocked TaskCompletionSource, cancellation-without-diagnostic, prior lease/mount disposal on replacement, stale/current artifact adoption, reload invariants, double dispose, dispose during in-flight inspection. WI-C5-05 flipped to Ready (C4-08 done). Validation: 15/15 new tests, full non-interactive suites green (1393+219+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-05 Done: animation pairing plus validated importer and preview options. ExternalModelImportOptions: positive finite UnitsPerMeter, named feature gates (MorphTargetsGate const; all off by default), per-target morph-weight ranges validated finite and ordered within [0,1]; WithUnitsPerMeter/WithFeatureGate return validated copies. ExternalModelPreviewOptions (record): model yaw/pitch/roll + translation, camera orbit/elevation/distance/fov, background + lighting presets (Neutral/Dark, Neutral/Studio), selected animation key, sample time, morph weights; Validate enforces finiteness across all numerics, positive camera distance, fov in (0,pi], non-negative sample time, sample-time-within-selected-duration, no sample time without a selection, morph weights only when the gate is enabled and only for declared targets within range (InvalidDataException before anything applies). Session: LoadAnimationAsync mounts an independent animation document (generation-checked like model loads, Animation-source diagnostics, SeparateDocument pairing cleared when the replaced document owned it); SelectAnimation resolves by stable C4 key against the model catalog or the separate animation catalog (duplicate display names stay distinct, SameDocument vs SeparateDocument recorded, sample time resets, descriptor duration validated); SetImportOptionsAsync stores options and reruns full inspection with re-created mounts (unit scale is baked into the mount's format selection; the animation document is re-mounted and its catalog re-inspected; option changes clear pairing since keys cannot be assumed across re-imports at new scale), publishes ImportOptions into every snapshot; SetPreviewOptions validates then republishes without reopening sources; ResetToDefaultsAsync restores canonical C4 import scale and preview defaults, clears pairing, reruns inspection, never touches source files. ExternalModelSnapshot extended with AnimationSourceDisplayName/AnimationPairing/ImportOptions/PreviewOptions (defaults canonical); ExternalModelReport + JSON carry pairing (document, source, key, name, duration, channels), import options (unitsPerMeter, enabled gates sorted, morph ranges sorted), and full preview corrections. Fixes found by tests: snapshot `with` publishes must explicitly carry mutated session fields (generation, import options, reset values) instead of inheriting stale values. 12 ExternalAnimationPairingTests: same/separate-document selection, duplicate names by key, unknown-key throw, null clear, replacement clearing invalid separate selection but keeping valid same-document, import reload remounts model+animation (4 mounts), invalid preview values throw before applying, preview-only update does not reopen sources, morph gate/range enforcement, reset, report carries pairing+options. WI-C5-06 flipped to Ready. Validation: 232 ReplaySketch.Tests (all Core external-model tests), 1393 Game.Tests non-interactive, 53 Mathematics, build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-06 Done: versioned external model request protocol. ExternalModelSourceRequest (AbsoluteRoot + normalized VirtualKey + FormatId; host-absolute paths only here and in outputs), ExternalModelViewport (positive width/height), ExternalModelRequest (schemaVersion const 1, generation, model + optional animation sources, ExternalModelImportOptions, ExternalModelPreviewOptions incl. camera/lighting/sample time/morph weights, viewport, optional OutputImagePath = report-only mode, required OutputReportPath). ExternalModelProtocolJson: deterministic camelCase + string-enum + omit-nulls serialization through explicit payloads, translation as float[3]; Deserialize enforces the exact schema version (InvalidDataException) and reconstructs validated option types (invalid ctor values fail at parse). ExternalModelRequestValidator: structured EXT Selection diagnostics without touching any game installation or source document - EXT100 schema version, EXT001 unsupported format (GLTF only), EXT102 non-normalized virtual keys (rooted, backslash, dot segments, empty/whitespace segments, drive separators), EXT103 missing/relative source roots, EXT105 non-positive viewport, EXT106 invalid preview options through the shared Validate (finiteness, distance, fov, morph gates), EXT110 output family (relative paths, existing directory targets, missing parent, duplicate image/report paths, image and report split across canonical parent directories, overwrite of either source file), EXT111 missing report path. 22 ExternalModelProtocolTests: full round trip of every documented option incl. morph weights and presets, byte-deterministic serialization, version rejection, separate roots, report-only, and every output validation case. WI-C5-07 flipped to Ready (C4-12 done). Validation: 22/22, build/format clean after group validation.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-07 Done: TestHarness external-model host. Program.Main dispatches --external-model-request before TestHarness.json loading and scenario construction via ExternalModelHost.RunArguments (exact-one value rule): exit 2 for missing/duplicate request arguments, 3 for unreadable request files, 4 for unparseable or invalid requests, 5 for operation failures, 0 on success. RunJson parses through ExternalModelProtocolJson (strict schema version) then ExternalModelRequestValidator; RunRequest re-validates defensively. Installation resolution happens only after validation (GameInstallation.FindAll over the Generals definition); game created headless with NoAudio. Mounts: independent ExternalAssetSourceMount instances per source with GltfImportOptions mapped from request import options; importer construction only through the internal ExternalFormatFactory under the existing friend-assembly access; missing model/animation documents are Selection-stage EXT002 failures rather than parse failures. Materialization through an external AssetLoadContext whose FileSystem is the model mount alone (never CompositeFileSystem with the install): relative C3 image paths can only resolve inside the external root; graphics/shaders/asset store come from the game host services. Binding validated once through ModelInstance.CreateAnimationInstance + Play (C2) with a local ConstantRandom. IExternalModelRenderStage seam with ExternalModelRenderInputs/Outcome; default stage returns a structured EXT300 Info not-rendered outcome after successful materialization. Success and failure reports written through ExternalModelReportJson; reverse-ownership disposal (animation, model, game) in finally on every path. C4 fixture matrix linked into ReplaySketch.Tests output via csproj Content link, resolved from AppContext.BaseDirectory. 13 ExternalModelHostTests: argument codes (2/2/3), validation-before-installation with CNC_GENERALS_PATH cleared (exit 4, failure report written), validation diagnostics surfaced, per-root mount isolation, animation-key resolution (selection/animation-source/null), static PBR materialization through the external filesystem (report eligibility + source hash + EXT300), cross-document binding by name (rigid-scene model + separate-root copy, SeparateDocument pairing in report), missing document (EXT002), malformed document (GLTF010 + failure report), injected render-stage throw (EXT999, failure report, no crash), external-texture-only-in-model-root materialization. WI-C5-08 flipped to Ready (C4a-10 done). Validation: 13/13 with install, full non-interactive suites green (1393+267+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-08 Done: deterministic external-model rendering and atomic artifacts. StandaloneModelCapture extended with explicit inputs (no behavior change for existing callers): StandaloneCaptureCamera (spherical orbit/elevation around the fitted transformed bounds center, explicit distance and vertical fov through Camera.SetLookAt + FieldOfView), StandaloneCaptureOptions with optional WorldLighting override and background color through a new instance RenderPipeline.ClearColor property (default unchanged). ExternalModelSceneRenderer (IExternalModelRenderStage): builds the post-import world matrix rotZ(yaw)*rotX(pitch)*rotY(roll)*translation (preview-only; vertices/skeleton/C4 basis untouched), evaluates the selected animation at exactly the requested sample time through fixed eight-sub-step animation-instance updates, discards one identical warm-up frame absorbing first-execution pipeline instability, captures through FrameCapturer into a staging sibling, and atomically replaces the final image; report-only requests (no OutputImagePath) return before allocating any render target or writing bytes. ExternalModelArtifactWriter: staging+replace publication, staging cleanup on failure, RemoveImage for report-replacement rollback, SHA-256 ComputeFileHash. ExternalModelReport/Json extended with ExternalRenderMetadata (viewport, animation key + sample time, PNG content hash + byte length; no staging or installation paths). Host publishes the success report last and removes a newly published image when report replacement fails; all failure reports go through the atomic writer. Program dispatch passes the real renderer. 12 ExternalModelRenderingTests + existing StandaloneModelCaptureTests: world-matrix composition identity/fixed order, writer atomic publish/failed-publish leaves final intact/no staging leftovers/remove-missing tolerance, report-only completes without PNG, successful render publishes both artifacts with matching hash+length metadata and recorded corrections, repeated identical requests produce identical PNG hashes (verified with real install), animated request records the fixed sample time, injected stage failure leaves failure report and no image. WI-C5-09 flipped to Ready. Validation: 12/12 with install, full non-interactive suites green (1393+276+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-09 Done: awaitable cancellable TestHarness preview client. SiblingBuildExecutableLocator (Core Services) generalizes LauncherLocatorService's sibling build-output convention (src-walk by project directory existence, configuration preference from the running base directory, bin/<config>/<tfm>/ search, platform .exe naming) behind Locate(projectName, baseDirectory = null); LauncherLocatorService.Locate delegates for OpenSage.Launcher with unchanged behavior. IExternalModelProcess/IExternalModelProcessFactory internal adapter: Start (UseShellExecute=false, redirected stderr, no window), bounded ReadStandardErrorAsync (64 KiB), WaitForExitAsync, KillTree (entireProcessTree on exactly the owned instance), Dispose; SystemExternalModelProcess wraps System.Diagnostics.Process. Core gained InternalsVisibleTo ReplaySketch.Tests for the fake seams. ExternalModelReport/JSON gained requestGeneration (echoed by the host from the request). TestHarnessPreviewClient (public IExternalModelPreviewClient): locates OpenSage.Tools.TestHarness through the sibling locator (EXT200 when absent), writes the serialized request as request-<lease>.json next to the validated artifact outputs, launches '--external-model-request <path>' directly, and validates exit code (EXT210 + bounded stderr in local detail, never in the message or serialized report), report presence (EXT211), parse validity (EXT212), generation echo (EXT213), and the requested PNG when an image output was requested (EXT214); report-only requests need no PNG. Cancellation registration kills exactly the owned process tree; the await path then waits for exit plus stderr drain and rethrows OperationCanceledException - no name-based kills, no double kill. Request file deleted on every path; caller lease and failure reports preserved; process disposed always. 15 tests: success path with argument and cleanup assertions, EXT200/201/210 (stderr only in detail)/211/212/213/214, cancellation kills once + awaits + disposes (gated fake), report-only success, plus locator tests (sibling discovery, configuration preference + any-config fallback, missing project, empty name, launcher delegation). WI-C5-10 flipped to Ready. Validation: 15/15, full non-interactive suites green (1393+291+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-19: WI-C5-10 Done: Core view model for the Model tab. IExternalModelFileSelector (separate model/animation selection, null = user cancellation). AsyncCommand (Core ViewModels): ICommand + awaitable ExecuteAsync with execution state and CanExecuteChanged, bindable Execute path continues failures into an UnhandledException event instead of async void; per-command CancellationTokenSource with Cancel. ExternalModelViewModel (INotifyPropertyChanged over one owned ExternalModelSession + injectable artifact store, file selector, main-thread dispatcher, preview client): projections for state, source names, structural summary lines, animation descriptors (session.GetAvailableAnimations added: model catalog + separate animation catalog union), sorted diagnostics merged with the latest preview-run diagnostics, selected diagnostic detail, eligibility, import/preview options, and latest preview artifact path/length; commands for choose/reload model, choose/clear animation, select clip by stable key, apply import options (NextImportOptions staging), apply preview options (NextPreviewOptions staging), reset, render, and cancel (cancels every active command). Render enabled only when Ready + eligibility.CanRender + idle (warnings never block); render builds the ExternalModelRequest from session state (model/animation roots from the selected paths, production store output paths, session generation), adopts the artifact on success, keeps preview failures as visible diagnostics, and treats cancellation as control flow; snapshot publications marshal through the dispatcher with stale-generation discard; Dispose cancels work, disposes the session first (observing its Disposed snapshot), then unsubscribes exactly once. 14 ExternalModelViewModelTests with fake selector/inspector/mounts/preview client and the real session + production store: inspection and summary publication, selector cancellation, warnings-visible + render-enabled, render gating, failed inspection disables render with EXT002, import reload vs preview-only no-reopen, render request shape + artifact adoption + lease accounting, render failure surfacing, render cancellation (async gated fake, no deadlock), stable-key selection incl. separate-document clips, reset, cancel-command token propagation, double dispose. WI-C5-11 flipped to Ready. Validation: 14/14, full non-interactive suites green, build/format/brace clean.
