WI-C4b-02 Done: importer enables the base texture stage when cache/texcache/<name>.texcache resolves through the import FS (C4a untextured fallback preserved), NIF V-up UVs flip to engine orientation, and the proof mounts textures.zip beside graphics.zip, decoding texcache DXT mips block-for-block into BC1/BC2/BC3 textures registered under their source .tga names. Two engine fixes found via the textured captures: NIF glossiness (0-100) must be scaled to the engine's shininess multiplier (raw 10 blews specular to full white), and EE2 winding matches neither engine front-face orientation so NIF materials import with culling disabled (now deliberate + documented instead of the accidental C4a leftover). Deterministic textured captures (galley 57.5%/bomber 60.2% chroma, zero flat-white); interactive stage-count test + 6 non-interactive installer tests; C4b marked Done.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-01 Done: NIF 10.1 KF block decoding in OpenSage.FileFormats.Nif. New blocks: NiControllerSequence (name, accumulation-root name, text-keys ref, controlled blocks as target-name/controller-ref pairs), NiTextKeyExtraData (name + (time, label) keys), NiKeyframeController (next/flags/frequency/phase/start/stop/target/data), NiKeyframeData (linear quaternion rotation keys, or XYZ Euler as order word + three float key groups, then Vector3 translation group + float scale group). New NifKeys.cs: NifKeyType enum (Linear 1/Quadratic 2/Tbc 3/XyzRotation 4/Constant 5), NifKey<T> (forward/backward tangents only on quadratic keys), NifQuaternionKey, NifKeyGroup<T>, internal NifKeyGroupReader (float/vector3 groups return null when empty; unknown type word or Tbc/Constant/non-linear quaternion => NotSupportedException naming block+field; XYZ rotation count must be 1). NifFile dispatch + ValidateReferences: text-keys ref must be NifTextKeyExtraData, controlled-block controller ref must be NifKeyframeController, controller data ref must be NifKeyframeData (InvalidDataException with block index + actual type). NifTestKeyframe test builders incl. key-type overrides for rejection tests; 11 NifKeyframeTests (full clip round-trip incl. empty Roots, quadratic tangent fidelity, empty groups, three bad-ref rejections, Tbc/Constant/unknown/quadratic-quaternion rejections). One pre-existing test updated: NifSceneGraphTests.UnknownBlockTypeFailsNamingBlockAndIndex used NiKeyframeController as its unknown-type fixture, now uses NiMorphData. Also fixed pre-existing main brace-rule violations in ZipFileSystem.cs (3 blank lines, separate commit) so the phase CI can pass. WI-C4c-03 flipped to Ready. Validation: 11/11 new tests, full non-interactive suites green (1480+320+53), build/format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-03 Done: pure NIF key-curve evaluation in OpenSage.Game/Content/Importing/Nif. NifKeyCurve.Evaluate(NifKeyGroup<NifKey<float>>, time): end-held linear/Hermite evaluation, segment-normalized Hermite with outgoing = first key backward and incoming = second key forward (NifSkope convention). NifRotationSampler.EulerToMatrix(x,y,z) returns the stored NifMatrix33 layout for column-vector Rz*Ry*Rx; SampleXyz(data, duration) builds the 6.3 time set (k/30 grid, duration, every source key time; deduped within 1e-6 s), evaluates the three Euler axes, composes via EulerToMatrix, converts to source-frame quaternions (positional transpose before CreateFromRotationMatrix since Matrix4x4 is row-vector), hemisphere-flips consecutive samples, and rejects steps >= 90 degrees (NotSupportedException naming angle + time). 7 NifKeyCurveTests: EulerToMatrix(2.3865, 0.5080, -1.1135) matches the real R_OAR14 stored rest matrix (dumped from nwg1_galley.nifcache) to 2e-4; three-turn linear spin => 31 samples at 36-degree steps in one direction (last sample is negative identity, compared via |dot|); Hermite midpoint vs hand-computed value; linear holds; single-key constant; time-set coverage exactly once; 90-degree step rejected. Validation: 7/7 new tests, full non-interactive suites green (1487+320+53), format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-02 Done: NIF node hierarchy preserved as engine bones. NifSceneConverter now returns internal NifSceneGraph(skeleton, subObjects): every unit-scale NiNode/NiLODNode becomes an ImportedBone depth-first root first (source names, nearest bone ancestor as parent, Galley 30 / Bomber 22 bones, skeleton origin Embedded); bone locals are the source locals conjugated by the source-to-engine map via new NifTransformConverter.CreateBoneLocalMatrix/ConjugateSourceToEngine (A = E^-1 L E; rotation conjugated by Rz90, translation rotated into feet), quaternion sign canonicalized like glTF. Shapes bake their transform RELATIVE to the parent bone (local*relativeToBone)*E, so composing bone rests reproduces the exact C4a world bake (E^-1 W_bone E * relative * E = W_shape * E); non-unit-scale nodes (and their whole subtrees) never become bones and bake into the nearest bone ancestor; a shape with no unit-scale ancestor throws NotSupportedException. NifModelImporter.ImportModel/ImportSkeleton share ReadNifFile; default single-bone skeleton removed. StandaloneModelCapture.ComputeEnclosingBoundingBox now accumulates rest-pose bone worlds (bones are parent-first) instead of using the local-only bone matrix, which is wrong under a real hierarchy. Tests: synthetic importer tests updated + 3 new (hierarchy/conjugation parity incl. real R_OAR14 rest matrix to 1e-4, scaled-subtree collapse, scaled-root rejection); Ee2NifImportTests single-bone asserts replaced with 30/22 bone locks (R_OAR14, prop_01, prop_02, sub-object parents), AssertBounds now computes the exact world AABB from baked vertices transformed by the accumulated bone rest chain (box-corner transforms overestimate rotated sub-objects and would break the locked 0.2 ft AABBs); NifTestBlocks.Node gained a rotation parameter. Static capture parity: Ee2NifProof regenerated on both old and new code; images differ by 0.8-2.5% edge pixels (threshold 12) with a 2px camera recenter from the corrected bounds, same chroma mix, identical validation guides. WI-C4c-04 flipped to Ready (02+03 done). Validation: 13/13 NifModelImporterTests, 4/4 Ee2NifImportTests (interactive), full non-interactive suites green (1472+320+53), format clean, brace check clean except pre-existing ZipFileSystem lines fixed on the group-1 branch.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-04 Done: NIF KF animation importer in OpenSage.Game/Content/Importing/Nif. NifAnimationKey parses <model-key>#kf=<archive-relative-kf-path> (null for malformed); NifAnimationImporter (IAnimationImporter, id NIF) resolves the model nifcache + the KF entry through the import FS (null when either is missing), buffers via MemoryStream, requires block 0 to be a controller sequence (InvalidDataException with the asset key), builds the skeleton through the card-02 ConvertGraph entry point, and names the animation after the KF stem. NifAnimationConverter enforces the full section 7 contract: exactly 'start'@0 + 'end'@D>0 text keys (duration from them), key times finite/in-range/non-decreasing at 1e-4, controller flags 0x2C + frequency 1 + phase 0 + null next/target refs, case-insensitive bone targets with duplicate/missing rejection, unit-scale validation (keys within 1e-4 of 1, then dropped), accumulation-root constancy within 1e-5 (ordinary channels when constant, NotSupportedException when varying). Channels: quaternion keys at source key times, XYZ via NifRotationSampler.SampleXyz at the resampled times, translation as X/Y/Z float channels, all Linear; rest-relative offsets follow the C4 rule with one deliberate deviation from the deep-dive's glTF-borrowed phrasing: rotation offset = Concatenate(sample, Inverse(rest)) (NOT Concatenate(Inverse(rest), sample)) because the runtime applies the offset BEFORE the rest (ModelBoneInstance.Matrix = offset * rest) and 'offset * rest == sample' is the locked acceptance criterion; translation offset = (sample - rest) rotated by Inverse(restRotation), matching glTF exactly. Also fixed the latent card-03 transpose bug: NifRotationSampler.ToQuaternion now positionally copies NifMatrix33 into Matrix4x4 (row-vector consistency), and the spin-test direction assertion flipped accordingly (stored Rz*Ry*Rx row-vector = negative axis-angle in System.Numerics). 29 NifAnimationImporterTests (offset reconstruction to 1e-4 against the real R_OAR14 rest, every rejection branch, malformed/missing nulls, accum-root constant + varying). Validation: 29/29 new tests, 7/7 NifKeyCurveTests, full non-interactive suites green (1519+320+53), format/brace clean.
2026-09-22: WI-C4c-05 Done: Ee2KfAnimationImportTests (interactive, 6 tests) lock the 7 DDF-bound EE2 clips through NifAnimationImporter. Descriptor test: all 7 clips import with KF-stem names, table durations (2.1667/1.0/3.0 s), exact channel counts (Galley 20: 12 oars Quaternion-only + ROOT and ROOT NonAccum with TranslationX/Y/Z; Bomber 16: all 4 targets full sets), per-target channel kinds; the unreferenced ab11_TwinEngineBomber.kf fails naming missing target prop_1. Runtime pose tests (headless TestGraphicsContext, no Generals install, ConstantRandom, zero-delta Update to refresh RelativeBoneTransforms): Galley Idle animated offsets stay identity through half the clip; Bomber Walk prop_01 turns 90 degrees (±0.5) between t=0 and t=1/12 s; Bomber TakeOff t=0 equals the rest pose except the root bone, which flight clips key to identity while root NonAccum carries the ground pose (rotation asserted different from rest); Bomber TakeOff 1.333 s root NonAccum world pose equals Walk t=0 pose. Channel structure was verified empirically against the installed archive, then locked. Validation: 6/6 interactive tests, full non-interactive suites green (1519+320+53), format/brace clean.
